With increase in temperature, $T_C$ is decreasing.

\begin{aligned}
T_C(0) &amp; =100 \mathrm{~K} \\
T_C &amp; =75 \mathrm{~K} \text { at } B=7.5 \mathrm{~T}
\end{aligned}

Hence, at $B=5 \mathrm{~T}, \quad T_C$ should lie between $75 \mathrm{~K}$ and $100 \mathrm{~K}$. Hence, the correct option should be (b).

By Ohm's law, \( V=I R \Rightarrow \frac{I}{V}=\frac{1}{R} \)<br/>Thus, the slope of I-V graph is reciprocal of resistance. In the given diagram,<br/>Slope of \( Q&gt; \) Slope of \( P \)<br/>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow \frac{1}{R_{0}}&gt;\frac{1}{R_{p}} \\
\Rightarrow R_{p}&gt;R_{o}
\end{array}
\]

